  "worked_solution": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\u230ax\u230b$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n\u230ax\u230b=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-2.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.5) & =\\frac{\u230a(-2.5)^{3}\u230b}{(-2.5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\u230a-15.625\u230b}{6.25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u230a-15.625\u230b=-16.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.5) & =\\frac{\u230a-15.625\u230b}{6.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-16)}{6.25} \\\\  & =-2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
